==Special attack==
[[File:Blood Infusion.gif|thumb|220px|A player performing the dual macuahuitl's special attack, ''Blood Infusion''.]]
The dual macuahuitl has a [[Special attacks|special attack]], ''Blood Infusion'', which costs 25% special attack energy, requires the full [[blood moon armour]] set to use, and takes 25% of the player's current [[Hitpoints]] (rounded down, meaning no damage is taken below 4 [[Hitpoints]]), regardless of whether you hit or miss.

In exchange, the special attack removes the sequential accuracy check, so both hitsplats roll accuracy independently for that attack, meaning a miss on the first one no longer guarantees a miss on the second. Each hitsplat's accuracy is also increased by 25%, and the player's maximum hit is increased by 25%, calculated before the total is split across the two hitsplats. Additionally, the [[Blood moon armour#Set effect|''Bloodrager'']] set effect is guaranteed to trigger if either hitsplat hits.{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/434286997360738305/1551904700293713971|date=2026-09-22|quote=> Costs 25% of your current HP to use, rounded down
Yes.

> Gives +25% accuracy on each splat, Gives +25% maximum hit
Yes.

> This seems to be calculated before the max hit is split across the two splats.
It is.
To avoid rounding down due to the split...
If the max hit had been 38, that becomes floor(38 x 1.25) = 47, which is split into 23 + 24, rather than floor(47 / 2) for both.

> The minimum hit mentioned in the blog did not make it into the game
I think that's correct. Although the weapon has a parameter on it calling for a min hit of "25%", that percentage appears to be applied to a starting value of zero.
Which really begs the question of whether I'm reading this correctly.

> The two splats rolls accuracy independently, missing the first splat doesn't guarantee a 0 on the second splat anymore
Yes.

> Passing accuracy on either splat guarantees the set effect
Yes.|archiveurl=|archivedate=|ctxquote=|notes=|name=}}

Within the [[Nightmare Zone]], the special attack will remove [[absorption]] charges if above 4 HP, dealing 0 damage to the player.

==Set effect==
When worn with all of the other pieces of the [[blood moon armour]] set, the player gains the ''Bloodrager'' set effect where the dual macuahuitl has a 33% chance upon a [[successful hit]] to attack one [[tick]] earlier than usual, allowing the player to attack again after 3 ticks. More precisely, a value 0-99 inclusive is rolled, and the set effect triggers if the result is 32 or below. If both hits are successful, it rolls twice and takes the lower of the two values, giving a 55.11%<ref><math>1-(1-33/100)^2</math></ref> chance to trigger the set effect.<ref name="Ash Regular attack"/>

It is possible for the set effect to activate even if one or more of the armour pieces are broken.

